# web/.env.example
# Copy to web/.env.local (git-ignored via the `*.local` rule in web/.gitignore) for local
# `npm run dev` overrides. No secret ever belongs here or in any VITE_*-prefixed value: anything
# reaching a VITE_* variable is compiled into the shipped bundle and public by definition
# (docs/security/secrets-policy.md).

# Dev-server-only proxy target for `/api/*` requests (see vite.config.ts `server.proxy`).
# Deliberately NOT VITE_-prefixed: it configures the Vite dev server process itself and is never
# bundled into client code. Point this at however you're running the API locally:
#   - infra/docker/docker-compose.yml `api` service: http://localhost:${API_HOST_PORT:-5000}
#   - `dotnet run` from backend/src/CMPlus.WebApi directly: whatever port it prints
API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:5000
